---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageClass: posts
templateEngineOverride: njk
---
{% from "partials/orgs.njk" import orgSummary %}
{#- Story layout: a quiet full-page frame for scroll-driven pieces.

    When to use it: an entry built around one or more `.kh-scrolly` regions
    (a pinned graphic beside prose steps). The standard post.njk apparatus --
    pulse strip, left rail with word count, topic tallies and contents, a lead
    screenshot above the teaser -- competes with a pinned graphic and pushes
    the prose into an offset column. Everything else should use post.njk.

    What a post must provide:
      - `layout: layouts/story.njk`, plus the usual post frontmatter (title,
        teaser, date, tags, topics; `image` + `image_meta` are optional).
      - Body content written as a sequence of top-level blocks. Each one sits
        in a single centred reading column unless it is:
          .kh-scrolly              -- a scroll-driven region; spans the page
                                      once its script adds .kh-scrolly--enhanced.
                                      A region may be the WHOLE body (one
                                      graphic pinned from the cover to the
                                      close): give it data-scrolly-cover with
                                      a selector for the cover below, and the
                                      script adopts the cover into the region's
                                      step column, leaving no-JS and RSS readers
                                      the plain title page. Blocks inside such
                                      a region that belong in the graphic
                                      column (an interactive, a screenshot)
                                      carry data-scrolly-panel; see
                                      _kh-scrolly.scss.
          .kh-bleed-out            -- a full-width plate (screenshot,
                                      interactive, wide figure)
          .kh-story-flow           -- optional closing chain of figures (an
                                      <ol> of node boxes joined by arrows);
                                      /story-flow.js counts them in, unless the
                                      chain sits inside an enhanced region, where
                                      the region's graphic is the ending and the
                                      <ol> is the RSS / no-JS version
      - Any script the regions need, loaded by the post itself.

    What it changes relative to post.njk:
      - Opening is a cover: breadcrumb + ref, title, teaser as the dek, one
        meta line. No pulse strip, no rail, no topic tallies.
      - `image` is shown as a closing plate after the body rather than as a
        lead screenshot above it. To close on something AFTER the plate (a
        final visual), set `story_plate: body` and place the plate in the
        body, either with {% include "partials/story-plate.njk" %} or with
        your own figure built from `image` / `image_meta` (a region may want
        it as a panel); everything then sits in the body, so the RSS feed
        carries it too. `image` still feeds listings, thumbnails and the
        JSON-LD either way.
      - Date, word count, topics, ref and contents move to a colophon at the
        end, ahead of the entry foot.

    Enhanced-only states before the script runs: the inline script below
    adds `kh-js` to <body> at first paint, and _kh-scrolly.scss hides the
    scrolly panels and static figures under `body.kh-js` until the region's
    script adds `.kh-scrolly--enhanced` (a 3s CSS fallback reveals them if
    it never does). No-JS readers never get the class, so nothing is hidden
    for them. Opacity only, so no layout shift.

    What it must keep in step with post.njk (other code reads these):
      - kh-entry-kind / kh-entry-date comments and the kh-entry-content
        start/end markers (scripts/compute-corpus-stats.mjs).
      - The JSON-LD block, feedback partial and entry-foot partial.
      - data-pagefind-ignore on every piece of apparatus.
      - footer.njk's `hasByline` list includes this layout. -#}

<script>document.body.classList.add('kh-js');</script>
{% if tags and ('impact-stories' in tags) %}<!-- kh-entry-kind:impact-story -->{% elif tags and ('posts' in tags) %}<!-- kh-entry-kind:blog -->{% endif %}
<!-- kh-entry-date:{{ date | dateDisplay('yyyy-LL-dd') }} -->
{%- set isImpactStory = tags and ('impact-stories' in tags) %}
{#- Document reference: same rule as post.njk. -#}
{%- set docRef = (collections.impactStories | impactStoryRef(page.url)) if isImpactStory else null %}
{%- set docRef = docRef or (page | docRef) %}
{%- set words = content | wordCount %}

<article class="kh-story">
  <header class="kh-story__cover">
    <p class="kh-breadcrumb kh-story__strap" data-pagefind-ignore>
      {% if isImpactStory %}<a href="/work">← Work</a>{% else %}<a href="/blog">← Blog</a>{% endif %}
      {% if docRef %}<a class="kh-doc-ref" href="{{ page.url }}" title="Permalink to this entry">Ref {{ docRef }}</a>{% endif %}
    </p>
    <h1 class="kh-font-headline kh-story__title">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if teaser -%}
    <p class="kh-story__dek">{{ teaser | emdash | safe }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <p class="kh-meta kh-story__meta" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <time datetime="{{ date | dateDisplay('yyyy-MM-dd') }}">{% if isImpactStory %}{{ date | dateDisplay('y') }}{% else %}{{ date | dateDisplay }}{% endif %}</time>
      {% if org %}&middot; {{ org }} {% endif %}&middot; {{ words | formatNumber }} words
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="kh-content kh-story__body">
    <!-- kh-entry-content:start -->{{ content | safe }}<!-- kh-entry-content:end -->

    {#- `story_plate: body` means the post places the plate itself (see
        partials/story-plate.njk), so it can close on something after it. -#}
    {% if story_plate != 'body' %}{% include "partials/story-plate.njk" %}{% endif %}

    {%- if comment != false %}
    {% include "partials/feedback.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}

    {#- Colophon: the apparatus post.njk shows up front, gathered at the end
        where it no longer competes with the opening. -#}
    <footer class="kh-story__colophon" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <dl class="kh-story__colophon-list">
        <dt class="kh-meta">Published</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ date | dateDisplay('yyyy-MM-dd') }}">{{ date | dateDisplay }}</time></dd>
        <dt class="kh-meta">Length</dt>
        <dd>{{ words | formatNumber }} words</dd>
        {%- set orgText = orgSummary(org) | trim if org else '' %}
        {% if orgText %}
        <dt class="kh-meta">Context</dt>
        <dd>{{ orgText | safe }}</dd>
        {% endif %}
        {% if docRef %}
        <dt class="kh-meta">Ref</dt>
        <dd><a class="kh-doc-ref" href="{{ page.url }}" title="Permalink to this entry">{{ docRef }}</a></dd>
        {% endif %}
        {% if topics %}
        <dt class="kh-meta">Topics</dt>
        <dd>
          <ul class="kh-story__topics">
            {%- for topic in topics %}
            {%- set parent = topic | topicParent %}
            {%- set child = topic | topicChild %}
            {%- set topicSlug = collections.topics | topicPageSlug(topic) %}
            <li>{%- if topicSlug %}<a href="/topics/{{ topicSlug }}/">{{ parent }}</a>{% else %}{{ parent }}{% endif %}{% if child %} <span class="kh-topic-child">{{ child }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </dd>
        {% endif %}
        {%- set tocEntries = content | tocEntries %}
        {%- if tocEntries.length >= 2 %}
        <dt class="kh-meta">Contents</dt>
        <dd>
          <ol class="kh-story__contents">
            {%- for entry in tocEntries %}
            <li><a href="#{{ entry.id }}">{{ entry.text }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ol>
        </dd>
        {%- endif %}
      </dl>
      {% include "partials/series-nav.njk" %}
    </footer>
  </div>
</article>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "mainEntityOfPage": {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://www.allaboutken.com{{ page.url | url }}"
  },
  "headline": {{ title | dump | safe }},
  "description": {{ (teaser or siteConfig.siteInformation.short_description) | striptags | dump | safe }},
  "datePublished": {{ date | dump | safe }},
  "dateModified": {{ (updated or date) | dump | safe }},
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": {{ siteConfig.siteInformation.author | dump | safe }}
  },
  {% if image -%}
  "image": ["https://www.allaboutken.com/images{{ image | url }}"],
  {%- endif %}
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": {{ siteConfig.siteInformation.author | dump | safe }}
  }
}
</script>

{#- The shared entry foot assumes post.njk's wide two-column grid. In a
    story it follows the centred colophon, so .kh-story__foot re-flows it:
    byline and onward reading in the reading column, the sequence drawing on
    the wide track. The kh-story class supplies the measure variables. -#}
<div class="kh-story kh-story__foot">
{% include "partials/entry-foot.njk" %}
</div>
